WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.074
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is wabi-sabi: the unfinished bowl. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.381
Settle into a position that can support both ease and alertness. Relax the muscles around your eyes and let the day become quieter.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.545
Follow the next inhale from its beginning, then the exhale to its end. Let the breath be natural, unforced, and entirely enough.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.028
Wabi-sabi finds beauty in what is worn, uneven and unfinished. Not in spite of those qualities, but because of them. Nothing becomes lovely by becoming perfect.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:05.118
A tea bowl thrown slightly off centre, glazed unevenly, its rim a little low on one side. It has been used for two hundred years, and that is why it is treasured.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.356
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.706
Find something in yourself you have been treating as a draft of someone better. Let it be finished as it is, at least for the length of this breath.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:24.499
I will leave some quiet here. You do not need to empty the mind. Notice what appears, release the story, and return to breathing.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:03.777
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:26.427
Let one imperfect thing stand today. The crooked shelf. The reply that was good enough. The day that went sideways and still ended.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:53.310
Take one fuller breath. Feel the space beyond your body and let your eyes open in their own time. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
